<title>FRANCE: Lyonnaise, Suez shares suspended.</title>
<headline>Lyonnaise, Suez shares suspended.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of French giant utility Lyonnaise des Eaux and conglomerate Cie de Suez were suspended on the Paris bourse on Friday, pending a statement later in the day expected to announce formally their plans to merge.</p>
<p>The announcement of the share suspension was made by the French stock markets' association SBF. The two companies are due to hold a news conference outlining their plans at 1630 GMT.</p>
<p>Lyonnaise des Eaux chairman Jerome Monod confirmed earlier in a radio interview with Europe 1 that the giant utility group planned to acquire Suez through a merger-takeover.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
